Export the CUDA pool-trim and graph-evict hooks through the backend registry:
ggml_backend_cuda_trim_pools / ggml_backend_cuda_clear_graph. The engine
resolves both dynamically via ggml_backend_reg_get_proc_address in
src/framework/core/backend.cpp, to hand cached device memory back to the driver
between models in a multi-model process without tearing a backend down.

PROVENANCE (dual parentage). Both parents carry this feature. Since 2026-09-23
this file IS parent transcribe.cpp's patches/ggml/0002-export-cuda-pool-trim-
and-graph-evict.patch (its body applied verbatim at transcribe.cpp's own ggml
pin 456172ec), replacing the audio.cpp-derived version this repo carried
before. The old version was defective, not merely different: it added
ggml_cuda_pool::clear() as a default no-op and never overrode it, so
trim_pools freed NOTHING on either pool class - the API existed and did no
work. transcribe.cpp's version implements it:

  - legacy free-list pool: clear() returns every cached buffer to the driver
    (the same reclaim the pool already performs for its own allocation on OOM).
  - VMM pool (the default on modern GPUs): clear() unmaps the mapped-but-unused
    tail of the VA reservation above the bump pointer. free() only rewinds the
    pointer, so without this a run's high-water mark stays resident until the
    context is destroyed. Everything below the pointer is live (free() is
    LIFO), so only the tail - a whole number of granularity chunks - goes.
    HIP keeps its reverse-order unmap bookkeeping in sync (ROCR-Runtime#285).
  - ggml_backend_cuda_clear_graph erases one cached CUDA graph by the same key
    cuda_graph() uses (cgraph->nodes[0]) - the eviction the 10 s time-based
    sweep would eventually do, but now, on an allocation-failure path. It is a
    no-op unless USE_CUDA_GRAPH.
  - both entry points tolerate a NULL backend (ggml_backend_is_cuda would
    dereference it).

Keep this file in sync with transcribe.cpp's copy: a change there is a change
here. The stream-priority hooks transcribe.cpp chose not to port live in 0008.

